    "project_template_level_name": "aif-y2-making-predictions-lesson7-choice2-2026 + template",
    "long_instructions": "You are building a nearest-neighbor classifier to authenticate paintings. You want to predict if an unknown painting is authentic, a workshop copy, or a forgery by comparing its lab-measured features to a catalog of previously examined (known) paintings, using nearest neighbors classification.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Create a new model using `KNeighborsClassifier`\r\n- Train the model with`model.fit`\r\n\r\nYou’ll complete TODO 3 and TODO 4 in the next level.\r\n\r\n💻 Coding Tip\r\n\r\nTo create a `KNeighborsClassifier`, call it and set `n_neighbors=1`, so that predictions are based on a single nearest neighbor:\r\n\r\n```\r\nKNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=1)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you’ve saved your classifier in a variable  called `model`, you can fit it to data with code like:\r\n\r\n```\r\nmodel.fit(train_inputs, train_outputs)\r\n```\r\n",
